  "version": 1,
  "comments": {
    "c1": {
      "anchor": "p-mermaid-drawings#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Mermaid Drawings",
      "excerpt": "Your words (Owen, 2026-11-18): \"new spell-ui component: `mermaid` drawing which",
      "text": "How hard to switch out to FA?",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-19T01:42:04.180Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "Icons",
      "offset": 5422,
      "edited": "2026-11-19T01:42:05.545Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-19T02:35:12.165Z",
          "html": "<p>Small: icons are in P37 now (<a href=\"#q55\">Q55</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Spell UI's icons are already Font Awesome 7 Free, as SVG, so the drawing hands Mermaid the page's own icons.</li>\n  <li><code>fa:fa-car</code> looks up a registered <code>fa</code> pack first and draws SVG; Font Awesome's font is only Mermaid's fallback, never needed.</li>\n  <li>Only the icons a diagram names are fetched, through <code>UI.icons</code>, so names match <code>&lt;ui-icon&gt;</code>.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c2": {
      "anchor": "p-mermaid-drawings#field-2",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Mermaid Drawings",
      "excerpt": "Your words (Owen, 2026-11-18): \"new spell-ui component: `mermaid` drawing which",
      "text": "I'm going to want ELK for the new ui-diagram component",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-19T01:42:18.369Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "12.0 ELK is built into",
      "offset": 5024,
      "edited": "2026-11-19T01:42:28.615Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-19T02:35:13.442Z",
          "html": "<p>ELK is now one shared, lazily loaded engine in P37 (<a href=\"#q56\">Q56</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>Mermaid 12.3's npm module doesn't copy ELK in: it imports <code>elkjs</code> lazily, as an ordinary dependency.</li>\n  <li>One loader, <code>ElkEngine</code>, imports the same file, so the build has one ELK chunk, loaded once per page.</li>\n  <li><code>&lt;ui-diagram&gt;</code> using it is todo <a href=\"#t115\">T115</a>, not queued.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c3": {
      "anchor": "p-mermaid-drawings#field-3",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Mermaid Drawings",
      "excerpt": "A new Spell UI component, <ui-mermaid> , draws a Mermaid diagram from the text i",
      "text": "ui-mermaid-diagaram",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-19T01:43:01.881Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "ui-mermaid",
      "offset": 27,
      "edited": "2026-11-19T01:43:02.929Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-19T02:35:14.579Z",
          "html": "<p>Renamed (<a href=\"#q57\">Q57</a>).</p>\n<ul>\n  <li>The tag is <code>&lt;ui-mermaid-diagram&gt;</code> everywhere in P37, Q50 to Q52, and its folder, docs page and tests.</li>\n  <li>In Spanish, <code>&lt;es-diagrama-mermaid&gt;</code>, with \"sirena\" among the names it's found by.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ]
    },
    "c4": {
      "anchor": "p-mermaid-drawings#field-3",
      "kind": "field",
      "label": "Mermaid Drawings",
      "excerpt": "A new Spell UI component, <ui-mermaid> , draws a Mermaid diagram from the text i",
      "text": "what are the attributes of the component?  \n\nI'd like to be able to change theme / light dark within the component with a TR menu button visible on hover.  Should have `Save as PNG` and `Save as SVG`",
      "by": "owenoak",
      "at": "2026-11-19T01:43:27.447Z",
      "status": "answered",
      "quote": "draws in Spell",
      "offset": 108,
      "edited": "2026-11-19T01:44:09.034Z",
      "replies": [
        {
          "by": "owenoak",
          "agent": "claude",
          "at": "2026-11-19T02:35:15.725Z",
          "html": "<p>Attributes plus a hover menu, as you picked (<a href=\"#q54\">Q54</a>); the full table is in P37's Goal.</p>\n<ul>\n  <li><code>source</code> (or the text inside), <code>theme</code> (<code>spell</code> or Mermaid's presets), <code>scheme</code> (<code>auto</code>, <code>light</code>, <code>dark</code>), <code>look</code>, <code>layout</code>, <code>seed</code>.</li>\n  <li><code>controls</code> shows the hover menu; <code>remember</code> names where the reader's pick is kept; <code>label</code> is what a screen reader says.</li>\n  <li>The hover menu switches theme and light or dark for that drawing, after <code>--ui-hover-delay</code>, remembered per drawing; words in English and Spanish.</li>\n  <li>Events: drawn and error. Read-only properties: <code>svg</code>, <code>diagramType</code>, <code>error</code>.</li>\n</ul>"
        }
      ]
    }
  },
  "on": {}
}
